From 3beff7aab246459cf1ddd5d2ae88b65dfad593ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abrus861 <abrus861@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 01:33:15 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] bluez5: backend-native: keep the transport when AT+BCS
 confirms the current codec

Some headsets (seen with HUAWEI FreeClip, and matching the reports for
HUAWEI FreeBuds Pro 5) send AT+BCC on every audio connection after the
first one, about 160 ms after the AG has started the eSCO connect.

The AG answers +BCS:<current codec>, the headset confirms with AT+BCS=<same
codec>, and the handler then (a) frees and re-creates the transport and
(b) emits codec_switched, which makes the device remove and re-create its
nodes.  Both close the SCO socket while its connect is still in progress.

The kernel answers the close with Create Connection Cancel (rejected by
the controller with 'ACL Connection Already Exists') and drops its
hci_conn, while the controller still completes the eSCO link.  The link
is now orphaned: 'SCO packet for unknown connection handle', and every
later Enhanced Setup Synchronous Connection fails with 'Synchronous
Connection Limit to a Device Exceeded' until the ACL is reconnected.

If the confirmed codec is the one already in use and a transport exists,
there is nothing to switch: reply OK and keep the transport and the nodes.
---
 spa/plugins/bluez5/backend-native.c | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/spa/plugins/bluez5/backend-native.c b/spa/plugins/bluez5/backend-native.c
index 7c5fcefa8..6241942ed 100644
--- a/spa/plugins/bluez5/backend-native.c
+++ b/spa/plugins/bluez5/backend-native.c
@@ -1239,10 +1239,22 @@ static bool rfcomm_hfp_ag(struct rfcomm *rfcomm, char* buf)
 			return true;
 		}

-		rfcomm->codec = selected_codec;
-
 		spa_log_debug(backend->log, "RFCOMM selected_codec = %i", selected_codec);

+		if (rfcomm->transport != NULL && rfcomm->codec == selected_codec) {
+			/* The headset re-confirmed the codec that is already in use (some headsets send
+			 * AT+BCC on every audio connection).  Keep the transport: freeing it here would
+			 * close a SCO socket whose connection may still be in progress, which leaves an
+			 * orphaned eSCO link in the controller and breaks all later SCO setups.
+			 * For the same reason no codec_switched event is emitted: the device would
+			 * remove and re-create its nodes, releasing the transport mid-connect. */
+			spa_log_debug(backend->log, "RFCOMM codec unchanged, keeping transport");
+			rfcomm_send_reply(rfcomm, "OK");
+			return true;
+		}
+
+		rfcomm->codec = selected_codec;
+
 		/* Recreate transport, since previous connection may now be invalid */
 		if (rfcomm_new_transport(rfcomm, selected_codec) < 0) {
 			// TODO: We should manage the missing transport
